.TH LRCM 1 "2026-08-16" "lrcm 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lrcm \- linux remote configuration management agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lrcm
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lrcm
clones a git repository containing Ansible playbooks and applies them to the
local machine. It targets Linux clients that cannot be reached from a central
management infrastructure: remote schools and universities, IoT devices,
unattended terminals, marketing displays and sensors.
.PP
On every run lrcm checks that the distribution and the Python version are
supported, takes an advisory lock so two runs cannot overlap, waits a fixed
plus a random delay, shallow-clones the configured branch into a temporary
directory, applies
.IR playbook.yaml ,
then
.IR <hostname>-playbook.yaml
if it exists, creates or removes its own
.I /etc/cron.d/lrcm_*
entries, and finally deletes the temporary directory and releases the lock \-
also when something went wrong.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-configfile " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the configuration from \fIPATH\fR instead of
.IR /etc/lrcm/lrcm.conf .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log lrcm's own progress: the clone, each playbook and each cron entry.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Log everything, including ansible's output and memory figures.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-cronjobs " " \fIBOOL\fR
Manage the lrcm cron entries. Defaults to true.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cronjobs
Equivalent to \fB\-\-cronjobs=false\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-delay
Skip the configured start delay. Intended for interactive runs.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Additionally send log records to syslog, under the \fBdaemon\fR facility.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success. Also returned when another instance holds the lock.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration or environment error: unreadable configuration, unsupported
distribution, Python too old.
.TP
.B 2
A step failed while working: the clone failed, or a playbook did not succeed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/lrcm/lrcm.conf
Configuration. Created from the shipped template on first install, and never
overwritten by an upgrade. Holds the git token, so it is mode 0600 and owned by
root.
.TP
.I /usr/share/lrcm/lrcm.conf.template
The commented template the above is seeded from.
.TP
.I /run/lrcm.pid
Advisory lock file that keeps two lrcm runs from overlapping.
.TP
.I /etc/cron.d/lrcm_hourly, /etc/cron.d/lrcm_daily, /etc/cron.d/lrcm_reboot
Cron entries lrcm creates and removes according to the \fBCRONJOB\fR section of
its configuration.
.SH LOGGING
All diagnostics go to standard error; lrcm writes nothing to standard output.
Each record carries an RFC 3339 timestamp with the local UTC offset. Without
\fB\-v\fR or \fB\-d\fR only warnings and errors are printed, so a successful
cron run stays silent.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run once against the configured repository without touching the cron entries:
.PP
.RS
.EX
lrcm \-\-verbose \-\-no\-cronjobs \-\-no\-delay
.EE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cron (8),
.BR crontab (5),
.BR ansible-playbook (1)
.PP
Full documentation at
.I /usr/share/doc/lrcm/README.md
and
.UR https://github.com/72itde/linux-remote-configuration-management
.UE .
